<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Hood River Meadows and Sahalie Falls</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:194-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.325400" lon="-121.635000"><ele>1380.0</ele><name>Hood River Meadows Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hood-river-meadows-sno-park (annex lot by the Nordic Center); confidence: high; pdf_page: 194; quote: Several trails and a Nordic Center are accessed from Hood River Meadows Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325375" lon="-121.636172"><ele>1379.5</ele><name>Sno-park access road gate</name><desc>source: OSM gate node 3965312266 on the access road (way 37579194) at the west side of the lot; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 194; quote: Hood River Meadows Sno-Park, reached by a turnoff on Highway 35</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.322430" lon="-121.636390"><ele>1366.3</ele><name>Opening to the meadows off the old highway</name><desc>source: west bend of OSM way 125243916 (old Highway 35), the point of the road nearest the east edge of OSM 'Hood River Meadow' (way 542533315); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 196; book_elev_ft: 4477; quote: From the opening to the meadows off the old highway, follow the road south as it climbs gently uphill past the falls</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.318260" lon="-121.640030"><ele>1396.8</ele><name>Sahalie Falls bridge</name><desc>source: OSM node 33427702, where way 125243916 (old Highway 35) crosses the East Fork beside OSM node 'Sahalie Falls' (45.31863, -121.64038); confidence: high; pdf_page: 196; quote: The falls are 1 mile from the sno-park and a climb of only 100 feet. The falls are viewed from a bridge on the road.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Hood River Meadows and Sahalie Falls</name><desc>1. Hood River Meadows Sno-Park -&gt; Sno-park access road gate: straight (medium), 0.06 mi | 2. Sno-park access road gate -&gt; Opening to the meadows off the old highway: osm (medium), 0.23 mi | 3. Opening to the meadows off the old highway -&gt; Sahalie Falls bridge: osm (high), 0.61 mi</desc>
